cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this code or these derived data, please cite it as below."
title: "Remifentanil and hyperalgesia reporting: FAERS + Canada Vigilance two-database disproportionality study"
abstract: >-
  Reproduction package for a head-to-head disproportionality analysis of remifentanil
  against fentanyl, sufentanil and morphine in the US FDA Adverse Event Reporting System
  (via the openFDA drug/event API) and the Health Canada Canada Vigilance line-listing.
  Five of seven prespecified opioid-induced-hyperalgesia preferred terms return zero
  reports in both databases, and no disproportionate reporting of hyperalgesia is
  observed for remifentanil relative to any comparator.
